<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Hepburn is a 73-year-old woman with essential tremor of the head, voice, and hands who returns for her subsequent annual wellness visit, two months after her six-month tremor review. She completed the health risk assessment before the visit. She takes propranolol extended-release 60 mg each morning and has missed no doses. Her hands are steadier with cups and pens, and since the occupational therapy visit seven weeks ago she uses weighted utensils, a lidded travel cup, and a thicker pen. The head tremor is unchanged and does not trouble her. She uses the breath-support techniques from voice therapy on stage. She has had no falls, emergency visits, or hospital stays this year, and no lightheadedness, wheezing, or low mood. She swims and walks most days. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Subsequent annual wellness visit</td></tr><tr><td>Safety events</td><td>No falls, emergency visits, or hospital stays this year</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Propranolol extended-release 60 mg daily; no over-the-counter medicines or supplements</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Essential tremor with head, voice, and hand tremor; hand tremor improved on propranolol</td></tr><tr><td>Functional status</td><td>Independent in all activities and instrumental activities of daily living, with adaptive aids for eating and writing</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Very good</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Busy with stage and screen work, which she enjoys; close friends and a long-time household assistant; no loneliness</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>Never used tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol and drugs</td><td>An occasional drink (AUDIT-C 1); no other drug use</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Swims and walks most days, about 45 minutes a day</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Regular meals; one cup of coffee in the morning</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Seven to eight hours a night; no vivid dreams on propranolol</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent; adaptive utensils and cup in use</td></tr><tr><td>Instrumental activities of daily living</td><td>Independent; her assistant handles correspondence when her handwriting tires</td></tr><tr><td>Home safety</td><td>Smoke detectors working; handrails on the stairs; no loose rugs</td></tr><tr><td>Falls</td><td>No falls this year</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>No hearing concern; reading glasses; no eye examination in the past two years</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>No concerns</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
