<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Subsequent annual wellness visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given. Depression, alcohol, cognitive, and fall-risk screens are negative. Ten-year cardiovascular risk is about 7 percent by the pooled cohort equations, with no diabetes, hypertension, or smoking. [S]<list><item>Next annual wellness visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Essential tremor (G25.0)</content>. Hand tremor improved on propranolol and with adaptive aids; head tremor unchanged and not bothersome. Heart rate 64 with no orthostatic drop. [S]<list><item>Continue propranolol extended-release 60 mg each morning.</item><item>Tremor review with TETRAS in about four months, and the yearly movement disorders review.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Voice tremor due to essential tremor (R49.8)</content>. Mild, and managed with voice-therapy strategies. [S]<list><item>Continue the strategies; botulinum toxin remains an option if it worsens.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, this season</td><td>Completed today</td><td>High-dose vaccine given today</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 given today; no further doses needed</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Dose 1 given today; dose 2 due in two to six months</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, this season</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended at her age; she will get it at the pharmacy</td></tr><tr><td>RSV vaccine</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Recommended at 75 and older, and from 50 with conditions that raise risk; she has none. Review at 75</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis booster</td><td>Due</td><td>No dose on record in the past ten years; to be given with the second zoster dose</td></tr><tr><td>Breast cancer screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Mammography every two years from 40 to 74; no mammogram on record in the past two years</td></tr><tr><td>Bone density (DXA)</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Recommended for women 65 and older; no prior scan on record, and her low body weight raises fracture risk</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>No screening on record in the past ten years. Options discussed; she chose a fecal immunochemical test, and a kit was given today. A positive test needs colonoscopy</td></tr><tr><td>Cervical cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not recommended after 65 with adequate prior screening and no high-grade lesion</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol screening and statin decision</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Total cholesterol 198, HDL 70, LDL 110, triglycerides 90 mg/dL. Ten-year risk about 7 percent with no risk factor, so a statin is not recommended; repeat in five years</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Recommended for overweight adults 35 to 70; BMI 19.5, and fasting glucose was normal in January</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time screening recommended for adults 18 to 79; no result on record; drawn with her consent today</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer and abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never used tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0; PHQ-9 3 in May</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol misuse screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 1; she was told that alcohol briefly eases tremor but is not a treatment for it</td></tr><tr><td>Cognitive assessment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Mini-Cog 5 of 5; MoCA 28 in January</td></tr><tr><td>Falls prevention</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Timed Up and Go 9 seconds; no falls; daily swimming and walking continue</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Whispered-voice test passed in both ears</td></tr><tr><td>Eye examination</td><td>Due</td><td>No eye examination in the past two years; she will book with her eye doctor</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: High-dose influenza vaccine, 1980-1981 season; Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine PCV20; Recombinant zoster vaccine, dose 1 of 2 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, general items for older adults (no essential tremor monograph) (2026); Medicare Wellness Visits (Medicare Learning Network) (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Tremor review in about four months. Second zoster dose and the Tdap booster in two to six months. Mammogram, DXA scan, and the hepatitis C result to be reviewed when back. Return the stool test kit within two weeks. Next annual wellness visit in one year. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.21" extension="2015-08-01"/>
    <code code="42348-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Advance directives"/>
    <title>Advance Care Planning</title>
    <text><paragraph>Voluntary advance care planning discussion of about 20 minutes, with her consent. She named a health care agent, and a health care proxy form was completed; the agent is recorded in the chart and is not named here. She said that what matters most to her is staying independent, keeping working, and being told plainly about her health so she can make her own decisions. She chose not to record specific treatment preferences today. The plan will be revisited yearly and with any change in her health. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>
    </structuredBody>
  </component>
</ClinicalDocument>
